                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game (\"hidden gem\") is supposed to be focused on getting lost and exploring, solving (some tricky, smart) puzzles and challenges (such as timed sequences and platforming sections). Maybe no big deal for skilled gamers! :) (You can’t rebind keys and invert axis.)\n\nThere are 3 main levels, divided into sub-areas. The game saves your items, but your location always goes back to the beginning of an area. The developer intent is to play through one area [or more] per sitting. So this can take 1-2 hours, or even more… But there are checkpoints within an area.\n\nWhat you get: Diversified level design (tropical island, desert, lava caves, underwater sections, snow-scape, etc.) with beautiful looking graphics (including day and night cycles), nice art style and lovely sound/music. (There is an option to hide the HUD, for taking screenshots! ;-)) \n\nVery kind and supportive developer, always responding to community feedback and constantly improving the game!",
